  "description": "The phrase 'thank you for allowing me into your country' is a common rhetorical device used in anti-immigrant rhetoric to imply that immigrants are unwelcome or that their presence is a burden. It often sets up a false narrative of gratitude while simultaneously implying entitlement or a threat to the host country's values.",
